<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Song of General Kim Il Sung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 김일성 장군의 노래, Kim Il Sung janggunui norae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-il-sung">Kim Il Sung</a>&quot; is a North Korean marching song composed by Kim Won-gyun in 1946, with words by Ri Chan; Kim Chaek, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>'s first Minister of Industry and Minister of National Defence, as a composer alongside Kim Won-gyun, the composer of the anthem &quot;Aegukka&quot;.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the early 1980s Kim Jong Il sought to reduce the song's importance in favour of the &quot;<b>Song of General Kim Il Sung</b>&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/aegukka">Aegukka (North Korea)</a></li><li><blockquote>Where the &quot;<b>Song of General Kim Il Sung</b>&quot; was sung at the beginning of public gatherings, &quot;No Motherland Without You&quot; was often sung at the end.</blockquote><a href="/songs/no-motherland-without-you">No Motherland Without You</a></li><li><blockquote>The &quot;<b>Song of General Kim Il Sung</b>&quot; is a North Korean marching song composed by Kim Won-gyun in 1946, with words by Ri Chan; Kim Chaek, North Korea's first Minister of Industry and Minister of National Defence, as a composer alongside Kim Won-gyun, the composer of the anthem…</blockquote><a href="/songs/song-of-general-kim-il-sung">Song of General Kim Il Sung</a></li><li><blockquote>…song glorifying the leader appeared then, and describes the spreading of such songs in the hardest years, to secure the regime, as a form of musical politics; Rodong Sinmun named it, with the &quot;<b>Song of General Kim Il Sung</b>&quot;, one of the two national songs of the country.</blockquote><a href="/songs/song-of-general-kim-jong-il">Song of General Kim Jong Il</a></li></ul></section>
